{"context":"The delivery lifecycle specification is the authority every other layer conforms to (§5.1): the lifecycle model, manifest contract, standard command contract, verification contract, and vocabulary, published as docs plus JSON Schema. It is authored in the Core repository (§5.2) and carries its own version line (A2). This ADR decides how the specification is published. Source: ADR-029-specification-publication-format.md Date:2026-08-03 Status:Proposed.","decision":"- **Dual publication.** The delivery lifecycle specification is published as human-readable documentation PLUS a machine-readable JSON Schema. The JSON Schema is the machine-readable authority: where docs and schema disagree, the schema governs (this is the §11.2 drift mitigation).\n- **Authored in the Core repository**, per §5.2 — there is no separate specification repository in v2.\n- **Engine-path-independent corpus.** The specification corpus is authored without referencing engine paths or Go internals, so a future re-home is a move, not a rewrite (§5.2 item 4; §11.2 re-home trigger).\n- **Conformance harness as a named deliverable** (EPIC-013): the Anvil Runtime's behavior is validated against the specification in CI; the same harness can validate any independent runtime implementation (","consequences":"**Positive:** the contract is consumable outside the engine; the engine and the specification are validated against each other (A1); standards and external runtimes implement a stable, published contract; conformance evidence is re-checkable.\n\n**Negative:** two artifacts (docs + schema) must be kept coherent — the schema is authoritative, docs describe it; publishing mechanics add release complexity (ADR-024); schema tooling is not yet selected (deferred).","alternativesConsidered":"Considered\n\n- **Markdown-only publication.** Rejected: not machine-checkable; drift between spec and engine becomes undetectable by CI; conformance cannot be objective (§11.2).\n- **Separate specification repository.** Rejected on the four grounds of §5.2: governance single-threading, conformance co-location, no external consumers yet, and co-location-is-not-conflation.\n- **Other interface-definition choices (Proto, OpenAPI, hand-rolled schemas).** Deferred: the format family is fixed (docs + JSO"}